WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.620 --> 00:00:04.580
If you're looking for the lowdown on the fifth
Rambo film, you're in the right place.

00:00:04.660 --> 00:00:08.940
Before you head out to see Sly Stallone lay
waste to some bad guys again, here's everything

00:00:08.940 --> 00:00:12.260
you need to know about what the soldier is
up to in ​Rambo: Last Blood.

00:00:12.640 --> 00:00:14.960
Remember: he'll give you a war you won't believe.

00:00:15.400 --> 00:00:18.140
"...death is coming."

00:00:18.820 --> 00:00:22.500
While the Rambo series is definitely one of
Stallone's babies, there are still a lot of

00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:24.980
other people helping to bring the latest story
to life.

00:00:25.300 --> 00:00:28.520
Adrian Grunberg is in the director's chair
for Last Blood.

00:00:28.520 --> 00:00:33.030
It's only his second feature film as director,
following the 2012 Mel Gibson vehicle Get

00:00:33.030 --> 00:00:33.760
the Gringo.

00:00:33.860 --> 00:00:38.260
However, Grunberg has served as an assistant
director or second unit director on several

00:00:38.260 --> 00:00:43.560
films since the '90s, including Apocalypto,
Jarhead, Man on Fire, and The Legend of Zorro.

00:00:43.760 --> 00:00:46.880
Last Blood's screenplay is credited to Matthew
Cirulnick.

00:00:47.240 --> 00:00:51.480
Like Grunberg, the writer doesn't have a ton
of credits to his name his most high-profile

00:00:51.480 --> 00:00:55.060
credit to date is as creator of the Amazon
series Absentia.

00:00:55.560 --> 00:00:58.500
Unsurprisingly, Stallone also had a hand in
writing the film.

00:00:58.969 --> 00:01:03.820
David Morrell receives the standard "based
on characters by" credit for his 1972 novel

00:01:03.829 --> 00:01:07.900
First Blood, though the author has clarified
that he's had no involvement with the Rambo

00:01:07.900 --> 00:01:09.580
films since the first three.

00:01:09.880 --> 00:01:13.660
We'll be able to see what happens in the new
one when it hits theaters on September 19,

00:01:13.670 --> 00:01:14.670
2019.

00:01:15.900 --> 00:01:18.560
Rambo has evolved quite a bit over the decades.

00:01:18.750 --> 00:01:23.500
What started as a somewhat quiet, psychological
exploration of the effects of war has turned

00:01:23.500 --> 00:01:28.040
into a massive spectacle of revenge and blood-soaked
slaughter as the films have progressed.

00:01:28.300 --> 00:01:32.440
Last Blood will continue to ratchet up the
body count when John Rambo takes on a violent

00:01:32.440 --> 00:01:33.500
Mexican cartel.

00:01:34.080 --> 00:01:38.920
Reportedly, the movie's plot will feature
John Rambo as a ranch hand in Arizona struggling

00:01:38.920 --> 00:01:42.400
with PTSD and keeping busy by taking odd jobs.

00:01:42.770 --> 00:01:46.180
He learns that the daughter of a long-time
friend has been kidnapped while partying in

00:01:46.200 --> 00:01:48.820
Mexico, and he crosses the border to rescue
her.

00:01:49.120 --> 00:01:53.300
He teams with a journalist who is investigating
a series of kidnappings, and the two uncover

00:01:53.300 --> 00:01:55.900
a sex trafficking ring run by a drug cartel.

00:01:56.160 --> 00:01:58.820
Naturally, he then goes Rambo on everyone
involved.

00:02:00.060 --> 00:02:03.820
From the look of things, Last Blood will feature
a slightly different tone than the series

00:02:03.820 --> 00:02:05.680
has featured in the last few entries.

00:02:05.960 --> 00:02:09.940
For starters, it seems like they are dealing
with the fact that Stallone is in his 70s

00:02:09.940 --> 00:02:14.420
in a smart way John Rambo looks to be going
back to his roots a bit with his tactics.

00:02:14.709 --> 00:02:18.700
The trailer shows off a series of traps that
the wily soldier has set up to fight off his

00:02:18.700 --> 00:02:22.440
enemies, utilizing the same guerrilla tactics
he used back in his heyday.

00:02:22.849 --> 00:02:26.940
It also looks to be leaning into the Western
motif, with an epic trailer remix of "Old

00:02:26.940 --> 00:02:29.540
Town Road" inexplicably playing throughout.

00:02:29.820 --> 00:02:31.860
You really can't get away from that song.

00:02:32.900 --> 00:02:37.040
Interestingly, Rambo: Last Blood looks to
have little to do with previous entries in

00:02:37.040 --> 00:02:37.760
the series.

00:02:38.040 --> 00:02:42.180
The film has been compared to Logan, the definitive
Wolverine movie, showing what happens when

00:02:42.180 --> 00:02:46.020
a pop culture hero stops adventuring so much
as he nears the end of his life.

00:02:46.520 --> 00:02:50.280
Going along with this theme, there aren't
many returning characters from previous Rambo

00:02:50.280 --> 00:02:51.800
films in this fifth entry.

00:02:52.180 --> 00:02:56.900
It makes sense: 2008's Rambo was set in Burma,
halfway across the world from the American

00:02:56.900 --> 00:02:59.579
southwest and Mexico settings of Last Blood.

00:03:00.060 --> 00:03:04.400
Obviously, the one common thread here is John
Rambo himself, Sylvester Stallone.

00:03:04.900 --> 00:03:09.260
Like Logan, it appears that Stallone's character
is still struggling with his past the things

00:03:09.269 --> 00:03:13.319
he's experienced as well as the things he's
done and this looks to be a chance for him

00:03:13.320 --> 00:03:15.340
to silence some of his inner torments.

00:03:15.740 --> 00:03:19.440
The story surrounding the war veteran has
evolved throughout the film series, so it

00:03:19.450 --> 00:03:23.120
will be interesting to see what Last Blood
adds to the backstory of John Rambo.

00:03:24.239 --> 00:03:28.549
Almost all of the cast of Rambo: Last Blood
is new to the franchise, but one in particular

00:03:28.549 --> 00:03:33.650
we need to point out is Sergio Peris-Mancheta,
who will play Hugo Martinez in the film also

00:03:33.650 --> 00:03:35.860
known as at least one of the movie's villains.

00:03:36.090 --> 00:03:40.540
The character has been described as the leader
of the cartel that Rambo crosses paths with,

00:03:40.540 --> 00:03:44.080
and it looks like he will make the hero go
through hell and back to win the day.

00:03:44.349 --> 00:03:49.300
The Madrid-born Peris-Mancheta is more well-known
to Spanish audiences than American ones.

00:03:49.310 --> 00:03:53.700
But American viewers might recognize him from
Resident Evil: Afterlife, the movie Life Itself,

00:03:53.700 --> 00:03:55.420
or the FX series Snowfall.

00:03:56.420 --> 00:04:00.600
There are plenty of other strong actors who
will appear alongside Sly Stallone in Rambo:

00:04:00.600 --> 00:04:01.100
Last Blood.

00:04:01.300 --> 00:04:06.200
Paz Vega will play Carmen Delgado, the journalist
who teams with Rambo to track down the kidnapping

00:04:06.200 --> 00:04:06.720
victims.

00:04:07.060 --> 00:04:10.260
You might have seen her before in projects
like The OA and Spanglish.

00:04:10.720 --> 00:04:14.700
Some of the other big names that stand out
include Oscar Jaenada from The Losers, The

00:04:14.700 --> 00:04:18.920
Shallows, and Pirates of the Caribbean: On
Stranger Tides and Louis Mandylor from My

00:04:18.920 --> 00:04:20.320
Big Fat Greek Wedding.

00:04:20.740 --> 00:04:25.200
Finally, one other cast member we're really
excited about is Adriana Barraza, previously

00:04:25.200 --> 00:04:28.040
seen in movies like Babel, Thor, and Drag
Me To Hell.

00:04:28.840 --> 00:04:32.620
If you've come late to the Rambo game, you
may not understand the significance of the

00:04:32.620 --> 00:04:33.900
title
"Last Blood."

00:04:34.320 --> 00:04:38.350
It works in a few different ways, but the
most obvious is what ties it back to the original

00:04:38.350 --> 00:04:38.840
film.

00:04:40.080 --> 00:04:42.340
"But the time has come to face my past."

00:04:42.980 --> 00:04:47.000
The first film didn't even have "Rambo" in
the title, instead like the novel it's based

00:04:47.000 --> 00:04:49.140
on simply being titled First Blood.

00:04:49.580 --> 00:04:53.560
The second film added the character's name,
bringing us Rambo: First Blood Part II.

00:04:54.020 --> 00:04:58.000
So it seems like this latest release is trying
to tie itself more to the tone of the original

00:04:58.000 --> 00:05:02.060
two films than the more over-the-top styles
of the third and fourth movies.

00:05:02.620 --> 00:05:05.920
It also could signal that this is Stallone's
last go as John Rambo.

00:05:06.220 --> 00:05:10.240
On the other hand, it seemed unlikely that
a fifth film would even happen, and Stallone

00:05:10.240 --> 00:05:13.920
has said he'd be glad to reprise the role
if Last Blood is successful.

00:05:14.240 --> 00:05:16.180
So don't take that title too literally.

00:05:16.420 --> 00:05:17.420
"New Blood," anyone?

